#. Tag: title
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid "Perspective Adjustment"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &digikam; <emphasis>Perspective Adjustment</emphasis> is a tool for "
"adjusting the image's perspective."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "Digikam"
msgstr "Digikam"

#. Tag: title
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this tool you can work on the perspective in a photograph. This is very "
"useful when working with photographs that contain keystone distortion. "
"Keystone distortion occurs when an object is photographed from an angle "
"rather than from a straight-on view. For example, if you take an image of a "
"tall building from ground level, the edges of the building appear to meet "
"each other at the far end. On the other hand you can use this tool to "
"introduce a new perspective that is not a face-on view but to give the image "
"a creative spin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Perspective Adjustment"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All perspective transformations are performed around a fixed point called "
"the reference point. This point is at the center of the item you are "
"transforming and is displayed by a red circle."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the perspective, use the square areas at the image corners for "
"dragging. The perspective preview is rendered automatically. On the right of "
"the dialog you'll find a set of information witch help you to control the "
"perspective change:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>New Width</guilabel>: show the new image width in pixels including "
"the empty area around the image resulting from the geometrical "
"transformation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>New Height</guilabel>: show the new image height in pixels "
"including the empty area around the image resulting from the geometrical "
"transformation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Top Left Angle</guilabel>: show the current angle in degrees at "
"the top left corner of the perspective area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Top Right Angle</guilabel>: show the current angle in degrees at "
"the top right corner of the perspective area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Bottom Left Angle</guilabel>: show the current angle in degrees at "
"the bottom left corner of the perspective area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Bottom Right Angle</guilabel>: show the current angle in degrees "
"at the bottom right corner of the perspective area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After applying the perspective adjustment, the image inevitably gets blurred "
"a little bit. For a single adjustment, the amount of blurring is quite "
"small, but two adjustments cause twice as much blurring as one, and there is "
"no reason to blur things more than you have to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: editor-transform-perspective.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have adjusted the perspective of an image there will be unpleasant "
"triangular \"holes\" at the corners. One way to fix them is to crop the "
"image with <menuchoice><guimenu>Transform</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Crop</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> Image Editor menu."
msgstr ""

